      <body>
         <entry xml:id="diplopoterin-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">דיפלופוטירין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">dyplwpwṭyryn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">diplopoṭerin</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant" opt="false">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false">דיפלה פוטירין</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">dyplh pwṭyryn</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">diplah poṭerin</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="diplopoterin-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>double-cup</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>διπλοποτήριον</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>מנת כוסם ר' ישמעאל בר נחמן מש' ר' יונתן 
                     <app>
                        <lem>כדיפלה פוטירין</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V">כפיילי פיטרין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1 Ox2">כפילי פוטירין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">כיפיילי פוטירין</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">51,3</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 535:2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פיילי פיטרין</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>The portion of their cup (Ps 11,6). R. Yishmaʾel b. Naḥman said in R. Yonatan’s name: Like a douple-cup.</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 85 [26c: 54]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">כבפיילי פוטירין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Ps 655 [445b: 26]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">כפייליפוטירין</term>)</note>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>[Vat 2] נכנס למרחץ וכיון שיצא הביאו לו 
                     <app>
                        <lem>פיילא פוטירין</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">פיילין של דיפלא פוטירין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">פולין של דיפלא פוטירין</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">10,7</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 83: [notes]</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פיילא פוטירין</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פיילין</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פולין</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>He entered the bath and when he came out, they gave him a double-cup.</quote>
                  </cit>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Composed of Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">διπλῆ</term> + <term xml:lang="grc">ποτήριον</term>. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 400b-401a</bibl>, <bibl type="modern">AC III 319a</bibl>. The reading <term xml:lang="jpa">פיילא פוטירין</term> is composed of Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">φιάλη</term> + <term xml:lang="grc">ποτήριον</term>, see Sperber, Cards. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow II 1140b</bibl> interprets <term xml:lang="jpa">פוטירין</term> as Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ποτήεριον</term>, sort of a shrub (Astragalus Poterium). The meaning here should then be “a double [portion] of poterion”.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>210b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
